# What running the suite and building the distribution leave behind.
#
# Bytecode caches appear the moment anybody runs the tests, and a build writes
# into `build/` and `dist/`. None of it is authored and none of it is
# reproducible byte for byte across interpreters, so an untracked-but-visible
# tree is how somebody commits a `__pycache__` without noticing.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments, wherever somebody puts one while working in this tree.
.venv/
venv/

# What the coverage measurement leaves behind. The data file is a database
# written by the run and the report is generated from it, so both are outputs
# of a command rather than anything anybody wrote.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage-report/
